## Reflection

I enjoyed this project because it focused on the relationship between security controls, business risk, and compliance rather than only the technical side of cybersecurity.

My previous professional experience involved working in regulated environments where documentation, process compliance, and maintaining accurate records were important. 
This exercise helped me see how those skills can apply within cybersecurity governance, risk, and compliance work.

It also gave me practice looking at an organization more broadly: identifying what protections are already in place, determining where gaps exist, and recommending improvements based on risk.

## More to Explore

Areas I would like to continue developing include:

- NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF)
- NIST SP 800-53 security controls
- Control testing and audit evidence
- Risk registers and risk treatment
- Third-party risk management
- Security policy development
- Mapping controls across multiple frameworks
